  "worked_solution": "The constant $A$ is the amplitude of the function. \n\nFrom the graph, we see that the maximum value is ${y}_{max}=2$ and the minimum value is ${y}_{min}=-4.$ Therefore, the amplitude is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{{y}_{max}-{y}_{min}}{2}=\\frac{2-(-4)}{2}=3.\n$$",
